{# Home-page hero (restyled to DESIGN.md § "Homepage" / design
   reference 5a): full-bleed cover photo behind the transparent site header (see .has-hero in
   header.css/base.njk), holding the headline block (orange 56×3 rule → H1 → intro) and the
   photo-credit line. The calculator card overlaps the photo's lower edge — its top sits on the
   photo, the rest extends onto white below.
   Desktop: the photo fills the viewport, headline + calculator centred in it (.hero__frame is
   display:contents there, so media/scrim/credit resolve against .hero__cover as a full-bleed
   layer). Phone: .hero__frame is a real box sized by the headline block, so the photo keeps a
   ~1:1 crop instead of being stretched to viewport height.

   src/assets/img/hero/home/ holds the chosen photo plus a couple of standby favorites; their
   records (source, license, credit) are in _data/homeHeroPhotos.json.
   TO SWAP: in that file, move the wanted record first and flag the others standby (dev server
   hot-reloads). #}
{% set heroPhoto = homeHeroPhotos.photos | credited("home hero") | first %}
{% from "partials/photo-credit.njk" import creditText %}

<section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
  <div class="hero__cover">
    {# Desktop only (hero.css): two flex-grow spacers straddle .hero__inner (this one above it,
       .hero__spacer--bottom below) so extra viewport height splits evenly top and bottom. The
       calculator wrapper reserves its longest state's height in CSS, so the headline never
       moves. Can't be ::before/::after on .hero__cover — those only attach at the very
       start/end of its children, not between specific siblings. #}
    <div class="hero__spacer hero__spacer--top" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="hero__inner">
      <div class="hero__frame">
        <div
          class="hero__media{% if not heroPhoto %} hero__media--placeholder{% endif %}"
          data-hero-media
          aria-hidden="true"
          {% if heroPhoto %}style="background-image: url('/assets/img/hero/home/{{ heroPhoto.file }}')"{% endif %}
        ></div>
        <div class="hero__scrim{% if heroPhoto.needsDarkerScrim %} hero__scrim--dark{% endif %}" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <div class="hero__content">
          <span class="hero__rule" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <h1 id="hero-heading" class="hero__heading">{% for line in site.tagline | splitSentences %}<span class="hero__heading-line">{{ line }}</span>{% endfor %}</h1>
          <p class="hero__intro">
            Korea's F-1-D Digital Nomad Visa allows you to live and work remotely from Korea for
            up to three years. Explore the regions to find the right environment for your stay.
          </p>
        </div>
        {% if heroPhoto %}
          {# Photo credit, rendered from the photo record's credit. Absolute (photo
             bottom-right) on desktop; in flow at the foot of the photo on phone, clear of the
             overlapping calculator. #}
          <p class="hero__credit">
            Photo source: {{ creditText([heroPhoto] | photoCredits) }}
          </p>
        {% endif %}
      </div>

      {# Calculator: real <form>, calculator.js calls eligibility.js and renders the
       caption itself into #calc-msg below. JS-only per CLAUDE.md — the
       <noscript> fallback sends no-JS visitors to the static thresholds table instead.
       Markup order here is free to change (calculator.js keys off data-* / element names, not
       DOM order); the comparison logic and its messages are frozen. #}
      <div class="hero__calculator">
        <div id="calculator" class="calculator-mount" data-calculator-mount>
      <noscript>
        <p class="calculator-mount__noscript">
          The eligibility calculator needs JavaScript. See the
          <a href="/visa-info/">visa income thresholds</a> directly instead.
        </p>
      </noscript>
      <form class="calculator-form" data-calculator-form autocomplete="off" novalidate hidden>
        {# Card title + subtitle (design reference 5a). Inline UI microcopy, like the other hero
           strings. #}
        <p class="calculator-form__title">Check your eligibility</p>
        <p class="calculator-form__note">Eligible regions depend on your age, income, and whether
          you bring your family. Nothing is stored.</p>
        <div class="calculator-form__row">
          <div class="calculator-form__field">
            <label for="calc-salary">Annual income, gross (KRW)</label>
            {# type="text" (not number) so calculator.js can format it with thousand separators as
               the visitor types; it strips the separators back out before the eligibility check. #}
            <input
              type="text"
              id="calc-salary"
              name="salaryKrw"
              inputmode="numeric"
              autocomplete="off"
              placeholder="e.g. 70,000,000"
              aria-describedby="calc-msg"
              required
            >
          </div>
          <div class="calculator-form__field calculator-form__field--age">
            <label for="calc-age">Age</label>
            <input
              type="number"
              id="calc-age"
              name="age"
              inputmode="numeric"
              min="{{ visaRules.additionalFacts.minApplicantAge }}"
              max="120"
              aria-describedby="calc-msg"
              required
            >
          </div>
        </div>
        {# Its own row on phone, directly above "Check eligibility"; on desktop CSS `order` drops
           it to a second line beside Clear. The whole <label> is the tap target (min-height 44px
           on phone, calculator.css) — not just the 17px box. #}
        <label class="calculator-form__field--checkbox" for="calc-has-family">
          <input type="checkbox" id="calc-has-family" name="hasFamily">
          <span>Bringing spouse or children</span>
        </label>
        <button type="submit" class="calculator-form__submit">Check eligibility</button>
        {# For a visitor who doesn't know their numbers yet (or wants to browse before committing
           to a check) — restores every region to open/active without needing a second, throwaway
           salary/age guess just to unlock the map. calculator.js wires this to the same
           applyResult() path a real "all eligible" tier would take. #}
        <button type="button" class="calculator-form__reset" data-calculator-reset>Clear</button>
      </form>

      {# Result-caption mount point — calculator.js owns all caption rendering here;
         korea-map.js only applies map state, it doesn't touch this element. Sits
         inside the card but outside the <form> so form.reset() and form.elements never see it.
         id="calc-msg" is what the fields' aria-describedby points at — aria-live="polite" means
         every result or validation message gets announced whether or not it's what moved focus. #}
      <p
        id="calc-msg"
        class="eligibility-result"
        data-eligibility-result
        aria-live="polite"
        hidden
      ></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="hero__spacer hero__spacer--bottom" aria-hidden="true"></div>

    {# Desktop only — the cover photo is full-viewport there, so a foot-of-photo nudge toward the
       map earns its place. A real anchor (CLAUDE.md), hidden on phone where the photo is
       a short crop and the map is already the next thing down. #}
    <a class="hero__scroll-cue" href="#map">Scroll down to explore Korean regions ↓</a>
  </div>

  {# Reference data for calculator.js — assembled at build time (see
     _data/eligibilityReferenceData.js), embedded here so the calculator needs no network
     request and no server. Exactly the referenceData shape eligibility.js expects. #}
  <script type="application/json" id="eligibility-reference-data">{{ eligibilityReferenceData | dump | safe }}</script>
</section>
